              return value.

              ssttppnnccppyy(3) is a more useful alternative to this function.

       ssttrrnnccaatt(3)
              Catenate the input character  sequence,  contained  in  a  null‐
              padded  fixed‐size  buffer, into a destination string.  The pro‐
              grammer is responsible for allocating  a  buffer  large  enough.
              The return value is useless.

              Do  not  confuse this function with ssttrrnnccppyy(3); they are not re‐
